# Do not copy this by hand — run `npm run setup`.
#
# It writes .env.local from the Supabase stack running on your machine and
# generates a SESSION_SECRET, so nothing below has to be filled in manually and
# no key is ever committed to this repository. The shape it writes:
#
#   SESSION_SECRET             generated per machine; signs the stubbed-user cookie
#   SUPABASE_URL               the "API URL" line of `supabase start`
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY  the "service_role key" line — server-only, bypasses
#                              RLS, must never reach a client component
#   DATABASE_URL_APP           direct Postgres as app_login for asUser() (spec 07a);
#                              no BYPASSRLS, so RLS actually applies on that path
#
# Local development only. Anywhere that is not a laptop, all four are different
# values and the session secret is a real one: openssl rand -hex 32
